  "$comment": "Where each Armoury module hangs on its gun (#310 build 5, ticket 321; art #364): Content's mount names, each a point in metres in the gun's barrel frame (origin the trunnion, the barrel at rest), so the modules turn with the barrel they ride. A bore point sits on #362's zones of the real gun (docs/art/bore-gun); the two modules that share a mount were authored to fit side by side at one point (docs/art/armoury). The long barrel's sleeve runs past the crown, so a muzzle module rides out to its end once the long barrel is bought. Turret points are #364's review positions on the auto guns at look 3; a 'muzzle' point counts from the barrel's tip, which moves with the barrel look, and a 'head' point stays on the cupola while the barrel turns. The TD named no ids on #310, so these are mine (as hull.front was ticket 315's), checked against the committed review renders.",
